	(text "LMR33630BDDAR? 24V solid, 3A, 1.2Mhz, cheap and well stocked...\nLMR41420Y - 24V, 2A, 1.1Mhz, cheap and well stocked.\nSY8303 - 24v solid, 3A, 500-2000k, cheap and well stocked.\nI still refuse to use non-synch buck in the year of our wonder, 2026\nUsing two of the same, would save me extended fees, ok for small orders?\nbut just an 1117 is better?\n\n2 of them means you can always have 3.3v regardless of bus voltage?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.534 137.668 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "22d8730e-853a-415e-9627-311b25ada8e6")
	)
	(text "5-24V in, with\n buck to 12\n buck to 5\n buck to 3.3\n passthrough\nas options for the led supply.\nseparate 3.3V ~ish supply for the esp32 itself.\njust an ams1117-3.3 for the esp32? could I live with myself?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 37.592 122.936 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "24c97331-1af1-4531-9a97-e6fd93c398e8")
	)
	(text "USB to anyone who wants it,\npower if it's better than what we have"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 25.146 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "40d1e14a-c3b4-4ed3-9f5b-b679796b64fc")
	)
	(text "Worst case, we run out of time, we just do a 5V buck for leds and then 3.3 for esp32,\nget shit _done_ and out the door. it's already sept 17, who am I fucking kidding."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 103.886 117.602 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6c909cf8-43a9-458e-b97e-16d8aa92879b")
	)
	(text "eh, esp32 wants them, ch58x has them internal, just slap em down"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.704 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "94abde92-0e76-482e-913f-b7659561c0ef")
	)
